WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.831
Environment-safe C starts with a basic
habit:

2
00:00:02.911 --> 00:00:05.301
treat environment variables as process
input.

3
00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:08.489
They may be useful, expected, and
operationally convenient,

4
00:00:08.569 --> 00:00:10.601
but they are not automatically trusted.

5
00:00:10.681 --> 00:00:14.506
A value should not drive sensitive
behavior until the program has parsed and

6
00:00:14.586 --> 00:00:17.036
validated it according to its intended
meaning.

7
00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.148
Read environment values deliberately.

8
00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:20.364
Copy them when needed,

9
00:00:20.444 --> 00:00:24.328
convert them into typed application-owned
configuration, enforce limits,

10
00:00:24.408 --> 00:00:27.516
and define what happens when values are
missing or malformed.

11
00:00:27.596 --> 00:00:31.361
The rest of the program should use the
validated configuration rather than

12
00:00:31.441 --> 00:00:33.832
repeatedly consulting raw environment
state.

13
00:00:33.912 --> 00:00:37.318
Avoid basing trust or privilege decisions
only on the environment.

14
00:00:37.398 --> 00:00:40.865
In services, helpers, scheduled tasks, and
privileged components,

15
00:00:40.945 --> 00:00:43.634
inherited state should be minimized and
documented.

16
00:00:43.714 --> 00:00:47.240
Use controlled configuration, verified
identity, explicit policy,

17
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.890
and least privilege for higher-impact
decisions.

18
00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:54.512
Constrain environment-derived paths,
search behavior, and child process inheritance.

19
00:00:54.592 --> 00:00:57.760
Prefer explicit trusted locations for
sensitive operations.

20
00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.991
Build child environments intentionally.

21
00:01:00.071 --> 00:01:04.314
Protect secrets from logging, diagnostic
exposure, and unnecessary propagation.

22
00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:06.904
Finally, keep the environment contract
visible.

23
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:09.495
Tests should cover malformed and missing
values.

24
00:01:09.575 --> 00:01:12.085
Review should trace every variable to its
effect.

25
00:01:12.165 --> 00:01:15.452
Documentation should list supported
settings and sensitivity.

26
00:01:15.532 --> 00:01:17.743
Operational controls should remove drift.

27
00:01:17.823 --> 00:01:22.186
These habits turn environment variables
from hidden process state into predictable,

28
00:01:22.266 --> 00:01:23.700
reviewable configuration.
